    "CD28",
    "CLEC16A",
    "ETS1",
    "HLA-A",
    "HLA-DQA1",
    "HLA-DRB1",
    "IL10",
    "IL2RA",
    "IL7R",
    "IRF4",
    "SOCS1",
    "STAT4",
    "TYK2"
   ],
   "n_shared_autoimmune_genes": 13
  },
  "verdict": "CONDITIONAL USE \u2014 DROP for MS disease association, KEEP as an islet/T1D comparator.",
  "justification": "pankgraph's disease axis contains exactly ONE disease (type 1 diabetes); MS appears nowhere, under MONDO, DOID or NCIT. So it cannot supply any MS gene-disease edge. However all 59 MS core genes DO exist as pankgraph Gene nodes carrying 16-644 triples each (pancreatic-islet expression quantiles for non-diabetic / T1D / T2D donors, open-chromatin gene-activity scores, BioGRID interactions, GO functional_association, eQTL fine-mapping). 13 MS core genes are ALSO on the curated T1D gene list (CD28, CLEC16A, ETS1, HLA-A, HLA-DQA1, HLA-DRB1, IL10, IL2RA, IL7R, IRF4, SOCS1, STAT4, TYK2), which makes pankgraph usable specifically as a shared-autoimmune / islet-context comparator, not as an MS evidence source."
 },
